lens:
Luxury art direction for jewellery e-commerce (Mejuri / Missoma / Monica Vinader calibre) with Indian fine-jewellery taste, round 5: elegance, typography, photography sequence and crops, spacing and grid, colour, hierarchy, copy tone, and whether a Rs 2,399 piece feels worth desiring.

G3 passes. fold.png, added.png, fold-ad.png, screens_1-4.jpg and measure.json (05:41:52-56) are newer than prototype.html (05:41:50, md5 a4a874df...), and my renders of an untouched copy agree: H1 399-427, facts end 562, bar 575, no console errors. fold-ad.png is byte-identical to fold.png (md5 d4ae18d6...), by the builder's choice. I found no G1 trip from this lens. A grep of the page text, alt text, aria labels, JSON-LD, title and meta description finds only the FAQ's 'Is it real silver? No...', which is a denial.

All six of my round-4 fixes landed and work: the set's condition is said once; the spec table's Fits row is 48px; each bag line has one job; Riya's tiles carry 32px marks with two-line captions; the card's prices are right-aligned and the ring's lines are split; the 320 bar has its air back. No round-4 change made things worse from this lens.

New findings, each checked on a variant copy: the inert ticks are drawn in the primary's solid ink; a content-free after-add card; a stiff set caption; one-word last lines; a grey smear where the bar's fade meets the footer; three plates on slide 5; and on tall phones a chin crop with an empty band under the facts.

Evidence is in /tmp/claude-0/-home-user/aaed4e78-f5ea-57f6-bb8a-ea8f2c0ecee0/scratchpad/r5art/out:
- probe.json: boxes, the text-style census and the colours in use; states.json and mock.json: card modes, bag text and fold boxes;
- s2x_00..06.png: the page as 2x phone screens; slide_0..6.png and gallery_r5.jpg;
- added_1.png, added_ring.png, card_y60/120/180/200/350/1700/2300.png, added_320.png;
- drawer_1.png, drawer_2.png, drawer_4.png, set_after.png, set_all.png, viewer.png, land_riya.png, folds_open.png, folds_open2.png;
- fold_320x568.png, fold_412x732.png, fold_390x844.png, fold_412x915.png and folds_r5.jpg; foot_fade_zoom.png; src_r5.jpg.
Fixes 1, 2, 5, 6 and 7 were built into a COPY, /tmp/claude-0/-home-user/aaed4e78-f5ea-57f6-bb8a-ea8f2c0ecee0/scratchpad/r5art/mock/prototype.html (mkmock.py), and compared in cmp_set_all.jpg, cmp_set_two.jpg, cmp_added_ring.jpg, cmp_card120.jpg and cmp_footend.jpg. Fix 4 was tried at runtime on that copy (tall.js, cmp_tall.jpg), as was fix 3 on the untouched copy (s5.js, cmp_s5.jpg). faq.js checked fix 6's selector. The prototype was not edited.

score_now is the weighted mean of the same criteria as rounds 1-4 (C1, C2, C7, C10, C12, C13, C14, C18, C19, C20): 412.5 / 46 = 8.97. I report 8.9 because three of the new faults sit on routine paths: the ink ticks after any set add, the one-word lines in the folds, and the smear at every page end. The critique is also written to /tmp/claude-0/-home-user/aaed4e78-f5ea-57f6-bb8a-ea8f2c0ecee0/scratchpad/pdp10/rounds/r5_art.json.

