Held. The full card is right (added_1.png, added_ring.png; 85-360, or 85-364 after the ring):
- the bracelet first, with ₹2,399 right-aligned;
- the ring's 'PVD rhodium' and 'Adjustable, US 5–9' on their own lines;
- 'Adds ₹659, not ₹999 / 10% off both';
- after + Add, 'Bag ₹3,058 · you save ₹340'.
The compact form keeps the size range (card_y60.png).

Two faults:
- Between the compact and the two-line forms sits 'nosug'. It is a 140px card that says only 'Added to your bag / Prism Rivière Bracelet ₹2,399', then a hairline with nothing under it, then two links (card_y120.png). It repeats the H1 directly beneath it and drops the next step, which the shorter two-line form says. A 360x640 shopper gets it after adding at scrollY 100-150, and a 320x568 shopper on a first add from the top of the page (cmp_320.jpg).
- '✓ Added' is a solid ink block that competes with the ink bar under it (added_ring.png).

fixes.change:
Replace L263 and L266 with:
.add[aria-pressed="true"], .add.done { background: transparent; color: var(--ink); border-color: transparent; text-align: right; padding: 0; }
.add[aria-pressed="true"]:active, .add.done:active { background: transparent; }

Keep unchanged:
- L264 (cursor: default);
- the tick and the label text;
- aria-disabled;
- the 88x44 box, so no row moves and nothing changes size under the finger.

Measured on a copy (mock/prototype.html; cmp_set_all.jpg, cmp_set_two.jpg, cmp_added_ring.jpg):
- the rows keep their heights;
- '✓ IN BAG' right-aligns with the price above it at x 344;
- the card's '✓ ADDED' right-aligns with the bracelet's ₹2,399 at x 333.

Replace L711 with:
var sc = $('#setcap'), inb = ALL.filter(function (k) { return bag[k]; });
sc.textContent = !s.q ? 'With the bracelet in your bag' : s.q === 1 ? 'With the ' + short(inb[0]) + ' in your bag' : 'With the ' + word(s.q) + ' pieces in your bag';

It reads:
- 'With the bracelet in your bag' with the bracelet alone, so the commonest path sees no change after the add;
- 'With the ring in your bag';
- 'With the two pieces in your bag';
- 'With the three pieces in your bag'.
Each fits on one line at 320.

